Ana (PM): quick flag from the design review — the right-hand help panel labels the section 'Deployment profile' but our docs use 'Serving config'. users got confused during the demo.
Tomas (Docs): thanks Ana. which panel path?
Ana (PM): Console > Models > Model X > Serve > help panel header reads 'Add deployment profile' but docs article title is 'Configure serving config'.
Priya - FE: that difference will break deep anchors. our panel generator maps to docs by canonical headings, so mismatches can land users in the wrong section.
Tomas (Docs): my suggestion: pick one canonical term. I prefer 'serving config' for docs. For the UI we can show 'Deployment profile (serving config)' while we transition. Also add canonical meta and anchors in the docs so the panel links map reliably.
Harper (A11y): a11y note: when the panel link jumps to docs we currently mutate the hash but do not move focus or announce the change. screen-reader users don't know content updated. We should close the panel, set aria-hidden on it, update the url, then programmatically focus the target heading.
Priya - FE: agreed. plan for click handler: close panel, set aria-hidden, then focus target with tabindex tweak. short snippet we'll include in PR:
```
panel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
panel.classList.remove('open');
const target = document.getElementById(targetId);
if (target) {
  target.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
  target.focus();
  history.replaceState(null, '', `#${targetId}`);
}
```
Tomas (Docs): i'll add an alias note at the top of the article: "Terminology: serving config (UI may show 'deployment profile')" and add explicit anchor ids for the Serve section. i'll also produce a short spreadsheet of UI terms that differ from docs.
Ana (PM): can we add a small link icon inside the panel next to headings that deep-links to the exact docs anchor? users expected that affordance in the demo.
Priya - FE: yes, we can add an icon. decision needed: same-tab vs new tab. i vote same-tab if we manage focus and aria-hidden correctly.
Harper (A11y): same-tab is fine. ensure the icon has an aria-label like "Open docs for Serve section" and visible focus styles. announce navigation with a polite aria-live message like "Opened documentation: Serve configuration".
Ana (PM): can someone file a concise ticket with acceptance criteria: 1) standardize terminology (docs canonical = serving config); 2) update panel copy with parenthetical alias; 3) add deep-link icon in panel; 4) close panel + aria-hidden + focus on navigation; 5) analytics event for doc-link clicks.
Priya - FE: filing ticket INFRA-4201 now — will include unit tests for focus and an e2e that verifies deep-link behavior.
help-bot: created INFRA-4201: "Serve panel + docs term harmonization and deep-link accessibility" assigned to Priya - FE, due in 10 days.
Tomas (Docs): i'll queue a copy PR and the term diff spreadsheet. thanks everyone :thumbsup:
